# operating characteristics of the v1 success criteria (two-sided 95% Clopper-Pearson)
# principle: P(pass | sound) >= 0.9, P(pass | doubled nominal error) <= 0.05;
# S1, a conjunction over the key null conditions, meets it as a whole; P(S1-S7 together | sound) >= 0.9

## Nominal rates (errors by cause, decided 2026-10-08; a sound validator's model after the first review,
## the rule nominals after the second, the cells after the third)
  Designed sizes: false SUPPORTED 0.025 (alpha/2: the effect test is two-sided at alpha, the
  direction checked afterwards); false NOT SUPPORTED (metric invalid) on a valid metric 0.1 (2 alpha:
  GATE 4's upper bound below delta_min alpha/2, GATE 5's negative control alpha, a silent positive
  control shown blind alpha/2); false NO DETECTABLE EFFECT 0.05 and explained by depth 0.05 (alpha, the
  TOST's size); NOT SUPPORTED against the direction where it is an error 0.025 (one tail). With pilot.json a card's
  rates are a sound validator's on its case, in the engine's verdict order (sound_model): GATE 5 at
  0.075, GATE 4 at the odds measured on the case, then the effect's outcomes as the oracle found them
  on the case's datasets (after an UNTESTED GATE 4 its explained-by-depth share); a blind, ambiguous or
  useless metric in the engine's order on them. Without a measurement (the scenarios below): the
  designed sizes of the routes open on the card and decisiveness 0.85. Every wrong outcome is counted
  in its own cell: S2 a false SUPPORTED per group of the cards outside S1 (N2's steps, N3, N4, N6a and
  N6b, N7, the real effects), S4 a false NOT SUPPORTED against the direction or explained by depth, S5
  metric invalid on a valid metric and S6 NO DETECTABLE EFFECT, each per stratum (real effects, nulls,
  blind or useless metrics); a cell's threshold uses, per card, the larger of the rate and the designed
  size. S3 is judged on every stratum (not N3 and N8), at the principle's tier or the floor's (a
  validator half as decisive fails); S7 allows no engine error. The joint requirement is checked with
  S1 at its design.

## S1 as a whole: the number of datasets per key condition (5 conditions)
  the rule first holds at n = 763; k* moves in steps, so it fails again at n = 769-785, 802-808 (up to 1000); the plan's 790 meets it
  S1 false SUPPORTED, key null conditions: 5 conditions x n = 790, each passes with at most 29/790 false SUPPORTED (upper 95% CP bound <= 0.0523); P(one passes | 0.025) = 0.9824, P(all 5 pass | 0.025) = 0.9151, P(a condition passes | 0.050 there) = 0.0465 — meets the principle
  given the background every dataset is an independent draw, so the counts are binomial and the above is
  exact; read beyond the background's donors (their shared donors as a random sample: beta-binomial, design
  effect deff; the run reports the realized deff of every primary criterion, above 1.5 a limitation):
    deff 1.0: P(all 5 pass | 0.025) = 0.915, P(a condition passes | 0.050 there) = 0.046
    deff 1.1: P(all 5 pass | 0.025) = 0.892, P(a condition passes | 0.050 there) = 0.054
    deff 1.2: P(all 5 pass | 0.025) = 0.868, P(a condition passes | 0.050 there) = 0.062
    deff 1.5: P(all 5 pass | 0.025) = 0.800, P(a condition passes | 0.050 there) = 0.085
    the principle holds up to deff 1.044 (the doubled side up to 1.044, the sound side up to 1.065)

## S3's tiers on a stratum of n establishable cards
  at d = 0.85: the floor's tier passes a sound validator with >= 0.9835 (what S1 at its design leaves of 0.9) from n = 18, the principle's from n = 115
  at d = 0.80: the floor's tier passes a sound validator with >= 0.9835 (what S1 at its design leaves of 0.9) from n = 23, the principle's from n = 77
  at d = 0.70: the floor's tier passes a sound validator with >= 0.9835 (what S1 at its design leaves of 0.9) from n = 31, the principle's from n = 42

